Stimuli for on003825 (Grootswagers et al. 2022 THINGS-EEG)
==========================================================

The 22,248 images referenced by each subject's events.tsv come from the
THINGS image database (Hebart et al. 2019). They are NOT bundled with
this BIDS dataset because the THINGS image archive is licensed for
research / non-commercial use and may not be redistributed without
explicit consent of the copyright owners.

How to populate this folder
---------------------------
Acquire `images_THINGS.zip` directly from the canonical THINGS project on
OSF: https://osf.io/jum2f/ (file guid `rdxy2`, ~5 GB). The unzip password
is published alongside the archive at https://osf.io/j6a3m. Unpack so the
final layout matches the events.tsv `stim_file` references:

    stimuli/
      <concept>/
        <concept>_<NN><b|n|s>.jpg     # 12 examples per concept × 1854 concepts
      stim-things_image.json          # BIDS stimulus sidecar
      README

After unpacking, run `python code/smoke_test.py` from the dataset root to
confirm every events.tsv `stim_file` resolves to an existing image.

License
-------
The THINGS image-database license (https://osf.io/52wrx/download) limits
use to research / non-commercial purposes and forbids redistribution
without consent of the copyright owners.

Citations
---------
- Grootswagers, T., Zhou, I., Robinson, A., Hebart, M., & Carlson, T.
  (2022). Human electroencephalography recordings from 50 subjects for
  22,248 images from 1,854 object concepts. Data in Brief.
  https://doi.org/10.18112/openneuro.ds003825.v1.1.0
- Hebart, M.N. et al. (2019). THINGS: A database of 1,854 object concepts
  and more than 26,000 naturalistic object images.
  PLoS ONE 14(10): e0223792. https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0223792
